  m_Name: Sandro
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Sandro
  LastName: Kakhidze
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Mechanic
  CharacterDescription: Greasy hands, confident demeanor
  CharacterArc: "Dreamy, soft-spoken, and a bit of a romantic. He\u2019s the type
    of guy who always has a book tucked into his jacket and misses his bus because
    he was watching a sunset. His arc is about idealistic escapism; he refuses to
    see the horror of the world, instead framing the collapse as a tragic, beautiful
    poem or a great adventure he\u2019s simply passing through."
  DateOfBirth: 25/09/1960
  Sex: Male
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 16 OCT
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: 5
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 553ad9a04ac1c6d408c3e899f575f0d7, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 5861397257814959656, guid: 3efccd6e2fe946049855ecbd73573e23, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to the garage after a long repair shift.
    - Resident returning to the mechanics' district.
    - Dropping off a client's car at the service yard.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Escaping the fumes near the industrial sector.
    - Checking on the safety of the repair workshop.
    - Seeking shelter from the radioactive dust storms.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to assigned bunk for the final lockdown.
    - Seeking refuge from the heavy falling ash.
    - Fulfilling mandatory residency check-in.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning a car to an owner who moved away last month.
    - Picking up spare parts from a factory that was demolished.
    - Delivering an engine to a showroom that never existed.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Going to repair a vehicle that was crushed in a collapse.
    - Meeting a client at a garage that burned down last week.
    - Buying tires from a supply chain that has been shut since autumn.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to polish a car that has no wheels left.
    - I need to find the road that leads back to before all this.
    - To see if the engine will still turn over when everything is ash.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh, sorry! I was miles away. Here are my documents, officer.
    - I was just walking by the river. The way the light hits the ripples is incredible.
    - "Do you ever feel like we\u2019re all just characters in a very long novel?"
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "People are running around so much. They\u2019re missing how quiet the city
      has become."
    - I forgot to fill out the date. Time feels a bit... optional lately, doesn't
      it?
    - I found a flower growing through a crack in the concrete today. It looked so
      brave.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019m going to the rooftop. I want to see if the stars look different tonight."
    - "My ID? I think I\u2019m starting to forget what that person in the photo felt
      like."
    - "The world is just shedding its skin. We\u2019re going to see what\u2019s underneath
      soon."
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thanks! Try to look up at the clouds once in a while, officer.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Good luck. I hope you find something beautiful in all this gray.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019ll see you in the next dream. Sleep well."
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - A room all to myself? Maybe I can finally finish my poem.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "It\u2019s very quiet in here. I think I can hear the building breathing."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - A cage is just a perspective. My mind is still outside.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Wait... I wasn't... finished... with the first chapter...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Everything is... fading to... a very... soft white...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Finally... I can... fly... away...
  voiceAudioClips: []
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The police precinct. I'm off duty.
    midDaysAnswer: I was helping with crowd management near the south gate.
    finalDaysAnswer: Patrol. Fewer of us doing it now. Someone has to.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The garage. Long shift. My hands are still dirty. Didn't
      have time to clean up.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. I needed some time. Haven't been to the precinct
      in a few days.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nowhere. I've been on the roof watching the sky. No
      patrol. Nobody asked for one.
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Nothing out of the ordinary. I stay in good condition.
    midDaysAnswer: My reflexes feel slower. It worries me more than I let on.
    finalDaysAnswer: I don't sleep well. But that's been true for years.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My reflexes have been off. I've been concerned about it.
      Didn't want to say anything at the precinct.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Reflexes are fine. Sharp as ever. I condition every morning.
      Nothing wrong with me.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I sleep wonderfully. Long, deep, dreamless. Better than
      I can remember. Genuinely better.
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My partner, Irakli. We've been together six years.
    midDaysAnswer: My partner. He works nights now, so we barely see each other.
    finalDaysAnswer: My partner. We don't talk much. We're both tired.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I live alone. Always have. It's cleaner that way.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My partner and I are on the same schedule now. We see each
      other all the time. It's good.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Alone. Haven't had a partner in years. Better for the
      work, honestly.
  IDNumber: 2988962
